<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Helmold of Bosau</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1120–after 1177</span> · <a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Helmold of Bosau was a German priest and chronicler in Holstein. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> Chronicle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavs">Slavs</a> describes the conversion and conquest of the Polabian and Baltic Slavs, the German settlement of their lands and the mission of his patron <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishop</a> Vicelin, and is a main source for Slavic paganism, including the cult of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/svantevit">Svantevit</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arkona">Arkona</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/helmold-of-bosau.jpg" alt="Helmold of Bosau" width="320" height="461" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown scribe of the 15th century · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Helmold_HL.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
